# ~/.gitattributes: line-ending rules (LF everywhere, CRLF for Windows batch
# files). Stops WSL/Windows checkouts showing every file as modified.
# Used by: git, via the symlink from scripts/dotfile-install.sh. Note that git
# only reads a *global* attributes file if core.attributesFile points at it,
# which .gitconfig does not set, so in practice this file mainly documents intent.
# Fate: becomes the new repo's own .gitattributes (docs/tasks.md, P1.02).

#https://code.visualstudio.com/docs/remote/troubleshooting#_resolving-git-line-ending-issues-in-wsl-resulting-in-many-modified-files
* text=auto eol=lf
*.{cmd,[cC][mM][dD]} text eol=crlf
*.{bat,[bB][aA][tT]} text eol=crlf